prefer-no-csd

// Nothing is spawned here. The session's daemons — the bar, notifications,
// wallpaper, idle management, clipboard history, the battery watch — are
// systemd user units (the packages' own waybar.service and mako.service,
// the repo's under config/systemd/user), bound to graphical-session.target,
// which niri.service reaches once the compositor is up; setup.sh enables
// them, and they are restarted, reloaded and read in the journal like
// any unit. The session environment is the login shell's — niri-session
// imports it whole — so PATH with ~/.local/bin and EDITOR are
// config/bash/profile, and binds and units name the bin/ scripts bare;
// the toolkits' Wayland switches are config/environment.d, read by the
// same user manager.
// XDG autostart needs no spawns either: systemd's xdg-autostart-generator
// runs /etc/xdg/autostart under this session.
